Z||000000||fiero_hunter85||08-31-2001||09:05 AM||||in a few dsays i am getting a 85 fiero GT that has a bad engine. i am probably going to get a 3.1 instead of another 2.8 but i do need someone to answer a question for me before i buy a 3.1.<P>do the 3.1 engines use the same computer wiring harness as the 2.8 or will i have to get the wiring harness too?  <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||MinnGreenGT||08-31-2001||09:09 AM||||We used the stock (87 GT) harness from my car for my 3.1  Everything should be attach as if it were a 2.8<P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/grngtsig3.jpg"> <BR>Medium Metallic Green 87 GT<BR>3.1L High Output<BR>4 Spd OD Tranny<BR>Open (read: Loud) Exhaust<BR>and More!<BR>-Rob Bartlett||||reg||1
Z||000002||fiero_hunter85||08-31-2001||09:26 AM||||ok thanx. after i get the car home i am going to have to go to the salvage yeard and find a good engine with low miles. i am going to have alot of fun with this fiero ||||reg||7
Z||000003||MinnGreenGT||08-31-2001||09:28 AM||||I believe that there are a few different versions of the 3.1L... I'm not sure exactly what the differences are, but mine was from a late-model (don't recall year) Chevy Lumina Minivan (FWD applications work best).  And it's worked great. Good luck.<P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/grngtsig3.jpg"> <BR>Medium Metallic Green 87 GT<BR>3.1L High Output<BR>4 Spd OD Tranny<BR>Open (read: Loud) Exhaust<BR>and More!<BR>-Rob Bartlett||||reg||1
Z||000004||terryk||08-31-2001||11:35 AM||||Right, the 90-95 U-van 3.1L is iron head and 8.9:1 compression (same as the Fiero). <P>The others are AL head so only the block and crank are usable with the Fiero heads. You will need to get U-van pistons for 8.9:1 or Camaro for 8.5:1.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Dave Gunsul||08-31-2001||11:49 AM||||Front wheel drive has the starter in the correct place the rear wheel drive engines don't. The aluminum headed engines won't work at all unless you put the Fieros heads on them because the accessories won't bolt up and the manifold is different. Also make sure that you are getting the right flywheel/flexplate for the 3.1. The 3.1 is internally balanced but the 85-87 Fiero engines are externally balanced. If you have an 88 then you already have the correct flywheel/flexplate but if you don't then you must use one from an 88 Fiero.<P>------------------<BR>Dave Gunsul<BR>N.I.F.E. member<BR>86 GT modified<BR>85 SE daily driver||||reg||4
